# Planning and Task Breakdown

{%- include "templates/.harness/skills-shared/objective-control/CONTROL." ~ harness_language ~ ".md.jinja" %}

Treat the plan as a directed execution graph. Declare the observable `START`, observable `GOAL`, all user journeys, nodes, edges, dependencies, interfaces, and failure transitions required for start-to-goal reachability. Every critical edge must belong to a complete path.

Before every phase and every item, emit: unchanged macro objective, `edge_id`, entry/exit nodes, observable deliverable, likely files, dependencies, and stable test IDs in all three classes: `functional`, `quality`, and `regression`. Acceptance names the input, expected output, execution surface, command, and evidence artifact. No execution begins before this preflight is `PRONTO`. Test IDs are not self-attestation: validation binds every ID to a command the ledger executes successfully.
